---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who writes Un-overengineering and why."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-11-02')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Trang, an engineer in Seattle. I build AI-powered systems for a living, and here I do the
		opposite: the smallest thing that works, using tools that are already on my phone or laptop.
	</p>
	<p>
		The rule is simple. No new app to install, no account to create. If a spreadsheet, a Shortcut,
		or the Notes app can do the job with a little AI in the gaps, that is the build.
	</p>
	<p>
		Every post is reproducible: you should be able to copy the file, link, or prompt and have it
		working the same day. Later posts extend earlier ones, so expect "part 2".
	</p>
	<p>
		Code and templates live on <a href="https://github.com/tduong191" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
			>GitHub</a
		>.
	</p>
</Layout>
